  "verifiedControls": [
    "The v4 allowance uses daily-context-pilot-4 while v1/v2/v3 remain in readback and report types. Failed dispatch, failed persistence, uncertain transport, replay and prior campaign status do not reset the per-operator current-version allowance.",
    "The same five case IDs and order, five model attempts, 5000000-micro conservative ceiling, 2800000-micro pre-transport reservation, 60000ms request deadline, model identity checks, Gemini Enterprise-only dispatch and Workflow zero-retry controls remain in effect.",
    "New claim guards are candidate-only and bind I1/square:saturn:sun, N1/nl-sun-03 and I2/trine:jupiter:mars to release 0.9.0 plus bounded local observed predicates. Full reviewed fact equality is enforced upstream; source IDs alone are not semantic proof.",
    "Actual member adapter and fallback bytes remain frozen separately from unchanged original benchmarks. The runtime fallback JSON differs from the prior commit only in materialVersion. Adapter/fallback versions remain 1, and hashes change when bytes change.",
    "Serving policy binds six exact raw-file hashes plus all five writer/material version fields. Old, missing, extra and stale policies fail closed. Missing rollout remains off, and provider, release, modes, render and review identities remain required.",
    "The full rollout configuration participates in the immutable Today cache identity. Local authored serving creates its own encrypted reading, saves the independent reflection and source links, survives reload/export and preserves the prior reading and feedback when rollback restores its cache branch.",
    "Production-path metadata retains shared adapter identity at report level and each case mode/source/runtime-fallback/original-benchmark identity at case level; rejected raw candidate and delivered complete fallback remain distinct.",
    "Original benchmark, original source bundle, member adapter, rollout loader, evaluator dispatch/reservation/capture, shared language writer, Today storage logic and Workflow implementation remain byte-for-byte equal to the prior commit except for the explicitly listed revision-4 sources. No prior report or pilot artifact was overwritten by this review."
  ],
